  "blocks": [
    {
      "id": "b000001",
      "kind": "heading",
      "start_line": 1,
      "end_line": 1,
      "raw": "# Native Tooltip Gallery\n",
      "level": 1,
      "title": "Native Tooltip Gallery"
    },
    {
      "id": "b000002",
      "kind": "blank",
      "start_line": 2,
      "end_line": 2,
      "raw": "\n"
    },
    {
      "id": "b000003",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "start_line": 3,
      "end_line": 3,
      "raw": "A C++23 LVUI application using iiGUI's own retained bubble widgets, native fonts, PanelMaterial and an iiSDKCore application entry point. No OS tooltip or Qt control is created.\n"
    },
    {
      "id": "b000004",
      "kind": "blank",
      "start_line": 4,
      "end_line": 4,
      "raw": "\n"
    },
    {
      "id": "b000005",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "start_line": 5,
      "end_line": 5,
      "raw": "Hover or focus either origin. The first bubble contains live labels and an interactive child; the second uses wrapped text. The origin keeps its own click behavior. Available-area, text, placement and delay inputs bind to one retained backend. Core owns background work and all tooltip deadlines.\n"
    },
    {
      "id": "b000006",
      "kind": "blank",
      "start_line": 6,
      "end_line": 6,
      "raw": "\n"
    },
    {
      "id": "b000007",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "start_line": 7,
      "end_line": 7,
      "raw": "Build and privately install with ./install.sh, passing the staged SDK package locations. [Usage and verification scope](docs/Usage.md) explains the runtime contract. Installation only compiles and copies artifacts. Applications, tests and the registered self-test remain deferred to the final whole-goal runtime batch.\n"
    }
  ],
